{"name":"Date Fruit Brown","hex":"#af642b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"date","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The fruit of the date palm, Phoenix dactylifera, somewhat in the shape of an olive, containing a soft, sweet pulp and enclosing a hard kernel. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The date palm."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The addition to a writing, inscription, coin, etc., which specifies the time (especially the day, month, and year) when the writing or inscription was given, executed, or made.","A specific day in time at which a transaction or event takes place, or is appointed to take place; a given point of time."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/date"},{"term":"fruit","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A product of fertilization in a plant, specifically:\n\nThe seed-bearing part of a plant; often edible, colourful, fragrant, and sweet or sour; produced from a floral ovary after fertilization.\nThe spores of cryptogams and their accessory organs.","The seed-bearing part of a plant; often edible, colourful, fragrant, and sweet or sour; produced from a floral ovary after fertilization."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To produce fruit, seeds, or spores."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fruit"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Date palm","blocks":[{"text":"Phoenix dactylifera, commonly known as the date palm, is a flowering-plant species in the palm family Arecaceae, native to the region from the Gulf States and Iraq to Pakistan and India. It is cultivated for its edible sweet fruit called dates. The species is widely cultivated across northern Africa, the Middle East, Australia, South and Southeast Asia, the coastal Mediterranean basin, and Southern California. It is naturalised in many tropical and subtropical regions worldwide. P. dactylifera is the type species of genus Phoenix, which contains 12–19 species of wild date palms."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Dates005.jpg/330px-Dates005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Date_palm"},{"title":"Fruit","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a fruit is the seed-bearing structure in flowering plants (angiosperms) that is formed from the ovary after flowering."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Fruit_Platter-_Seasonal_Fruits.jpg/330px-Fruit_Platter-_Seasonal_Fruits.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fruit"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/%D7%93%D7%A7%D7%9C_%D7%AA%D7%9E%D7%A8_%D7%9E%D7%A6%D7%95%D7%99_%D7%97%D7%AA%D7%9A_%D7%92%D7%96%D7%A2_%D7%93%D7%9E%D7%95%D7%99_%D7%A2%D7%A5_%283%29.jpg/500px-%D7%93%D7%A7%D7%9C_%D7%AA%D7%9E%D7%A8_%D7%9E%D7%A6%D7%95%D7%99_%D7%97%D7%AA%D7%9A_%D7%92%D7%96%D7%A2_%D7%93%D7%9E%D7%95%D7%99_%D7%A2%D7%A5_%283%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/%D7%93%D7%A7%D7%9C_%D7%AA%D7%9E%D7%A8_%D7%9E%D7%A6%D7%95%D7%99_%D7%97%D7%AA%D7%9A_%D7%92%D7